                [ 'p', 'xTool puts the emphasis on simplicity: it describes the M2 software as intuitive with templates, says the F2 takes four steps from idea to product, and mentions beginner-friendly software with one-click autofocus for the S1 education version. You place the design on the material with a camera (M2, F2, P3) or with Pin-point™ positioning (S1).' ],
                [ 'p', 'Most of the learning goes into matching power and speed. For xTool Selected materials, xTool provides parameters in its Material EasySet library, and some come with a QR code card that a camera-equipped machine reads to apply the settings straight away (xTool names the P and F series). Start other materials with a test grid on an offcut. Set aside the first days for safety training and testing.' ],
